cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "ods: transmissibility-based operating deflection shapes from shaker tests"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Lee
    given-names: Daniel Eunbum
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/daniel-eunbum-lee/ods"
abstract: >-
  Operating deflection shapes (ODS) from shaker random-vibration tests, computed from H1
  transmissibility against the control accelerometer, with coherence, three views of the motion
  (absolute, relative to the table, elastic), peak picking, and a standalone interactive viewer.
  Implemented in Python and in MATLAB, checked against an exact cantilever-beam solution.
keywords:
  - operating deflection shape
  - transmissibility
  - shaker test
  - random vibration
  - structural dynamics
